      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 1800s, Scotts Hill thrived as a stop on the main stagecoach line between Clifton and Jackson.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scotts_Hill%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A tornado in May 1917 and a fire in October that same year nearly wiped out Scotts Hill’s businesses and homes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scotts_Hill%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Scotts Hill College opened in 1896 but closed around 1917, reflecting the town’s brief higher‑education experiment.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scotts_Hill%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The town’s public water system began operating in 1957, modernizing utilities for its residents.",
